\value{
Each \code{go_*()} function returns a graph object of the same
  class as its name; \code{add_*()} functions return the modified figure.
}
\description{
Each box spans from quartile 1 (Q1) to quartile 3 (Q3). The second
quartile (Q2, i.e. the median) is marked by a line inside the box. The
fences grow outward from the boxes' edges, by default they span +/- 1.5
times the interquartile range (IQR: Q3-Q1), The sample mean and standard
deviation as well as notches and the sample, outlier and suspected
outliers points can be optionally added to the box plot. The values and
positions corresponding to each boxes can be input using two signatures.
The first signature expects users to supply the sample values in the `y`
data array for vertical boxes (`x` for horizontal boxes). By supplying an
`x` (`y`) array, one box per distinct `x` (`y`) value is drawn If no `x`
(`y`) vector is provided, a single box is drawn. In this case, the box is
positioned with the trace `name` or with `x0` (`y0`) if provided. The
second signature expects users to supply the boxes corresponding Q1,
median and Q3 statistics in the `q1`, `median` and `q3` data arrays
respectively. Other box features relying on statistics namely
`lowerfence`, `upperfence`, `notchspan` can be set directly by the users.
To have plotly compute them or to show sample points besides the boxes,
users can set the `y` data array for vertical boxes (`x` for horizontal
boxes) to a 2D array with the outer length corresponding to the number of
boxes in the traces and the inner length corresponding the sample size.
}
\details{
\code{go_box()} and the nested object constructors below create validated
graph objects (named lists). Every property is checked against the
plotly.js schema when an object is created or modified (see
\code{\link{plotly_obj-modify}()}). \code{add_box()} creates an object
and adds it to a figure.

Nested objects documented here:
\describe{
\item{\code{go_box_hoverlabel()}}{\code{box.hoverlabel}}
\item{\code{go_box_hoverlabel_font()}}{\code{box.hoverlabel.font}: Sets
the font used in hover labels.}
\item{\code{go_box_legendgrouptitle()}}{\code{box.legendgrouptitle}}
\item{\code{go_box_legendgrouptitle_font()}}{\code{box.legendgrouptitle.font}:
Sets this legend group's title font.}
\item{\code{go_box_line()}}{\code{box.line}}
\item{\code{go_box_marker()}}{\code{box.marker}}
\item{\code{go_box_marker_line()}}{\code{box.marker.line}}
\item{\code{go_box_selected()}}{\code{box.selected}}
\item{\code{go_box_selected_marker()}}{\code{box.selected.marker}}
\item{\code{go_box_unselected()}}{\code{box.unselected}}
\item{\code{go_box_unselected_marker()}}{\code{box.unselected.marker}}
}
}
\examples{
go_box(x = 1:3, y = c(2, 1, 3), marker_color = "red")
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{go_figure}()}, \code{\link{add_trace}()}
}
